{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790732128,"nonce":"KwPvFyqxKf7pEPqN7EA9FfDyy28=","message":"GNU/Linux retained-RSS component fixed by 7d1a2cd6725b09545e8f5ab1addc68b84427450e.\n\nTieredRuntime now calls glibc `malloc_trim(0)` after initial lowering/code generation and the compiler repeats it when the last queued optimization releases its scratch modules. Other allocators and non-GNU targets remain unchanged.\n\nNUC A/B at current main 7e2e935c, release zylua built with `llvm-backend`, `ZYLUA_LLVM=1`, official `files.lua`, sampled from `/proc/\u003cpid\u003e/status` at the `[ZYLUA] compile` boundary:\n\n- before: 832,492 KB immediately after compile; 1,017,456 KB near exit; 1,093,752 KB overall peak; compile 9,069 ms\n- after initial trim only: 286,940 KB immediately after compile; 513,896 KB near exit\n- after initial and scratch trims: 271,120 KB immediately after compile; 503,540 KB near exit; 1,086,240 KB overall peak; compile 9,027 ms\n\nThis removes about 548 MiB after initial compile and about 502 MiB near exit without a measurable compile-time regression. The overall ~1.04 GiB peak is unchanged because the HIR and lowering data are still live at that point; lazy body lowering remains in df39517. macOS allocator fragmentation also remains part of this issue.\n\nValidation:\n\n- `cargo check -p zyntax_compiler --features llvm-backend`\n- `cargo check -p zyntax_embed`\n- `cargo test -p zyntax_compiler --test body_retention`\n- `cargo test -p zyntax_lua --test memory_pressure -- --nocapture` (10 programs, no growth failures)","files":null}]}